1
00:00:07,426 --> 00:00:12,061
-==www.RagBear.com==-
是, 首相  第2季第2集

2
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:23,402
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:25,384 --> 00:00:30,459
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=-
翻译: smapwestlife
校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:35,741 --> 00:00:39,120
官方保密

5
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,750
好 各位 今天的议程是审核
Gentlemen, we're here to consider security clearance

6
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:46,912
我前任的回忆录的最新一章
for the publication of my predecessor's memoirs.

7
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,128
副检察长
Solicitor General.

8
00:00:48,128 --> 00:00:51,237
对 各位知道 我们已经通过了1至7章
We've already approved chapters 1 to 7.

9
00:00:51,272 --> 00:00:53,964
我看没有理由不通过第8章
I see no reason to withhold approval for 8.

10
00:00:53,964 --> 00:00:57,304
等等 我觉得有些材料很成问题
There is some highly questionable material.

11
00:00:57,304 --> 00:01:00,392
哪些?      好 就从211页说起
Such as? Well, page 211, for a start.

12
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,051
不过是"行政事务大臣在内阁支持"
It only says, "The Administrative Affairs Minister supported

13
00:01:06,051 --> 00:01:08,774
"扩建塞拉菲尔德核燃料厂"
the expansion of Sellafield in Cabinet,

14
00:01:08,774 --> 00:01:13,556
"却又公开反对"      说的是我 我就是行政大臣
"but spoke out against it in public." I was the minister.

15
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:17,713
问题是 这不算泄密      可它不实啊
The point is it's not a security leak. But it isn't true.

16
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:22,078
文章本身确实很震撼 可恕我直言 首相
The documentation is fairly impressive, but with respect,

17
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,145
如果他诽谤您 只能出版之后告上法庭
if he's libelled you, it's a matter for the courts,

18
00:01:25,145 --> 00:01:27,278
出版前的安检委员会管不着
not for the Security Clearance Committee.

19
00:01:27,278 --> 00:01:31,990
怎么能让这种指控传出去 还不止211页
We can't have such accusations. It's not just page 211.

20
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:37,359
224页又有个恶毒指控 说我停止化工厂计划
On 224, about my stopping that chemical-plant project

21
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:40,114
是害怕媒体的空穴来风
because of a baseless press scare.

22
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:43,670
更站不住脚的一段出现在231页
Then there's an indefensible passage about me on page 231.

23
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:48,436
231页 "哈克关心选票更胜于原则"
Oh, 231. "Hacker was more interested in votes than principles,

24
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:53,390
"一见风声不对 拔腿就跑"
"running for cover at the first whiff of unpopularity.

25
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:57,951
"他提升了内阁平均年龄 却降低了平均智商"
"He raised the average age of Cabinet but lowered the average IQ."

26
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:03,794
谢谢 汉弗莱 我们都看过这章了
Thank you, Humphrey. We've all read the chapter.

27
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:07,009
对 可首相 我说过 我对他的话不置可否
As I said, I'm not supporting or defending him,

28
00:02:07,009 --> 00:02:09,405
可这确实不算泄密
but it's not an actual security breach.

29
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:12,518
再说 第5章也泄漏了 我们也没管
Chapter 5 got leaked and we took no action.

30
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,684
第五章高度赞扬了
Oh, well, chapter 5 was very complimentary about

31
00:02:14,684 --> 00:02:16,242
我跟库朗谈成的合同
my getting the Kumran contract.

32
00:02:16,242 --> 00:02:17,831
还有我的电脑保安规章
about my computer security guideline

33
00:02:17,831 --> 00:02:20,124
这里面的机密信息一样多
It had as much confidential material

34
00:02:20,124 --> 00:02:22,394
您甚至没发起泄密调查
and you never had a leak inquiry.

35
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:27,270
这章谁都可能漏给媒体嘛
Well... anybody could have leaked that chapter to the press.

36
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,191
谁都可能
Anybody.

37
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:36,433
我说 第8章就连标题...      "吉姆哈克的双面人生"
even the title of chapter 8 "2 Faces Of Jim Hacker."

38
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,795
这总不算秘密吧
Er, that's not a secret, surely.

39
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,825
抱歉 我觉得有安全隐患
I think there are security implications.

40
00:02:43,825 --> 00:02:45,431
塞拉菲尔德造的是核燃料
Sellafield is nuclear.

41
00:02:45,431 --> 00:02:47,545
可主管塞拉菲尔德的能源大臣
The Energy Secretary has seen the chapter

42
00:02:47,545 --> 00:02:49,721
也看过了 他也没意见
and he says he has no problems.

43
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,334
他当然没问题 里面管他叫
No! It describes him as the

44
00:02:52,334 --> 00:02:54,691
内阁最能干的大臣 又抹黑我一次
ablest minister in Cabinet. Another slur on me.

45
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,714
这不能入罪      我们挑明了说
It isn't actionable. Let's be clear.

46
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:01,077
我们有权拒绝出版 对吧?      是有权
We have the right to refuse publication. We have.

47
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,464
可如果他们无视我们 硬要出版
If they publish anyway,

48
00:03:02,464 --> 00:03:06,064
我的法律意见是 别指望靠法庭制止
we'll have no hope of stopping it through the courts.

49
00:03:06,099 --> 00:03:08,798
那只能指望出版社了      用什么理由?
Lean on the publishers. On what grounds?

50
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,269
国家利益      我已经解释了...
National interest. I've already...

51
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:14,696
这是无耻下流 国家利益岂能容忍
It's obscene filth. It cannot be in the national interest

52
00:03:14,696 --> 00:03:16,390
取笑国家领导人...
to ridicule the national leader.

53
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:21,999
我是说...破坏国家领导层公信力
I mean... undermine confidence in the national leadership.

54
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,913
第8章绝不能出版 好吗?
Chapter 8 must not be published, right?

55
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:34,118
好啊 伯纳      不太好 汉弗莱爵士
Well, Bernard? No, not very, Sir Humphrey.

56
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:38,151
首相看过了吗?
Has the PM seen that yet?

57
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:41,098
我不知道 不过"今日头条"播了摘要
They quoted it on "Today".

58
00:03:41,098 --> 00:03:42,953
他吃早餐时应该听见了
He'd have listened to it while he had breakfast.

59
00:03:42,953 --> 00:03:45,434
我也听说了 他被人当早餐吃了
I heard it. They had HIM for breakfast.

60
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,752
是啊 最受欢迎的是
They had fun with,

61
00:03:46,752 --> 00:03:49,188
"吉姆哈克提高了内阁平均年龄"
"Jim Hacker raised the average age of the Cabinet...

62
00:03:49,188 --> 00:03:51,478
"却拉低了平均智商" 是啊
(BOTH) "...but lowered the average IQ."

63
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:58,432
说实话 是挺有意思      确实不假 可是 另一方面...
it is rather amusing. Yes But on the other hand...

64
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,990
我知道 你怎么解释这次泄漏?
I know. Have you any explanation for this leak?

65
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:05,118
不是我干的 汉弗莱爵士      当然不是你
It wasn't me. Of course it wasn't you!

66
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:08,750
泄漏这一章对你对我都没好处
It's hardly in your interest or mine to leak THAT chapter.

67
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:12,629
不光是第8章本身 还有他想封杀它的事
it's the report that he tried to suppress it.

68
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:15,243
所以只能是与会的人干的
The leak came from someone at the meeting.

69
00:04:15,243 --> 00:04:16,609
早上好 汉弗莱爵士
Good morning.

70
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:21,151
他为什么这么想?      他有没有...已经...
What makes him think that? Is he... er...? Has he...

71
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:26,153
新闻办挤着全国一半媒体 等他回话
Half of Britain's press corps are here waiting for his response.

72
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:29,073
才一半?      另一半在打电话
Only half? The other half are on the phone.

73
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:31,231
境外媒体也注意到了
The foreign press have picked it up.

74
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:34,870
申请采访的有"世界报" "华盛顿邮报"
I've had interview requests from "Le Monde", the "Washington Post",

75
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:37,838
还有"时尚女装"
and "Women's Wear Daily".

76
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,207
你看他会作何反应?
How do you think he'll take it?

77
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,468
我们就快知道了
We're just about to find out.

78
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,152
嗯?
Well?

79
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:01,192
嗯? 说话啊
Well? Well, say something.

80
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:07,991
早上好 首相      早上好 首相
Good morning, Prime Minister. Good morning, Prime Minister.

81
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,499
看见了吗? 你是宣传秘书 比尔
Seen this? You're my press secretary, Bill.

82
00:05:10,499 --> 00:05:12,563
你知道这是灭顶之灾
It's a catastrophe!

83
00:05:12,598 --> 00:05:15,472
出于尊重 首相...      一点也不尊重 汉弗莱
With respect... With no respect at all!

84
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:21,237
不尊重国家机密 不尊重国家利益 不尊重国家领导人
No respect for confidentiality, national interest or the leader!

85
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,834
不可原谅 谁泄漏的?      问谁去?
Who leaked it? Who can say?

86
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,471
就问你 你最好有个答复 我要求马上追查
You can say and you'd better say! I want this traced at once!

87
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:30,464
一定是昨天与会的某个人
It must've been somebody at the meeting.

88
00:05:30,464 --> 00:05:32,187
我这就发起泄密调查
I'll set up a leak inquiry.

89
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:36,388
我不要泄密调查 我要找出谁干的
I don't want a leak inquiry. I want to find out who did it.

90
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:41,188
首相 发生泄密的时候 通常没人想知道谁干的
One normally doesn't want to find out who's responsible

91
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:44,079
万一是内阁成员就麻烦了
in case it turns out to be one of the Cabinet.

92
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,504
只有副检察长和我
The Solicitor General and I were the

93
00:05:45,504 --> 00:05:48,708
两名内阁成员出席 不会是他 检察官从不泄密
only ministers present. Law officers never leak.

94
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,318
再说对他也没好处
He had nothing to gain,

95
00:05:50,318 --> 00:05:52,706
也不是我 剩下都是公务员
it wasn't me and all the rest were officials.

96
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,178
我要一路告上法庭去
I will pursue this through to the courts!

97
00:05:55,178 --> 00:05:58,220
首相 您得给我个回话 媒体都在等着
The press are all waiting.

98
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:01,230
4家电视台要求采访 还有11家广播电台
There are four requests for TV interviews and eleven for radio.

99
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:04,314
绝了 上周我千方百计告诉他们
Marvellous. Last week, I was dying to tell them

100
00:06:04,314 --> 00:06:07,799
我如何缓和英苏局势 没人要听
about my achieving detente with the Soviets.

101
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:11,919
这下倒好 都跟一堆鹫鹰似的撵上来了
Now this happens and they charge in like a herd of vultures.

102
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,389
不是一堆 首相
Not herd, Prime Minister.

103
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,114
跟一堆鹫鹰一样...
(CLEARLY) Charge in like a herd...

104
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,669
鹫鹰不论堆 它们论群
Vultures don't herd, they flock.

105
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,794
而且它们不是撵 它们...
And they don't charge, they... er...

106
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:30,677
它们怎样 伯纳?      它们...
What do they do, Bernard? They... er...

107
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:38,351
坐下 伯纳
Sit down, Bernard.

108
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,989
媒体怎么就不能为国家着想?
Why can't the press support Britain?

109
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:46,994
干嘛非要揭丑闻 怎么不写写我们的成就?
Why do they muck-rake? Why can't they write about our successes?

110
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:51,392
比如...      比如我缓和了对苏关系
Like... er...? Well, like my detente with the Soviets.

111
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:56,714
苏联政府确实松口了些 可没什么实质举动
There are noises from the Kremlin, but nothing concrete.

112
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:59,269
就会有的啊      很抱歉 首相
It's going to. I'm sorry.

113
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,433
可我必须给他们个说法
I have to tell them something

114
00:07:01,433 --> 00:07:05,208
关于您试图封杀前首相回忆录的事
about you trying to suppress your predecessor's memoirs.

115
00:07:05,208 --> 00:07:09,278
很好 私下跟他们说 "首相亲信表示"
Talk to them off the record. "Sources close to the PM."

116
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,635
不要署名      好
Say nothing attributable. Right.

117
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:15,190
就说 他对我的描述谎话连篇
Say that what he said about me is a pack of lies.

118
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:19,911
您是说..."拔腿就跑"那些?
you mean running for cover and that sort of thing?

119
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,957
对      问题是 这是作者的意见
Yes. The problem is, it is the author's opinion.

120
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:26,429
发表意见不能叫做撒谎
We can't call him a liar for an opinion.

121
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,848
那就说谎言是
Well, say that it's a pack of lies

122
00:07:28,848 --> 00:07:31,545
我在内阁支持核燃料工厂
about my supporting Sellafield in Cabinet

123
00:07:31,545 --> 00:07:33,431
而又公开反对那件事
but speaking against it in public.

124
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:37,388
好 可问题是 这也不算假      闭嘴 伯纳
Er, yes, but  it is sort of true. shut up, Bernard.

125
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,710
可这怎么能叫谎话连篇呢?
How do we say it's a pack of lies?

126
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:44,190
首相的回忆和前首相的大相径庭
The PM's recollection is at variance with his predecessor's.

127
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:47,670
然后说内阁记录支持我的说法
Then say the Cabinet minutes vindicate me completely,

128
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:54,029
不幸的是 根据30年解密原则 它们25年内不能公开
owing to the 30-year rule, they can't be disclosed for 25 years,

129
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,636
使得他的书不仅不实 更不公平
which makes his book deeply unfair as well as untrue.

130
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:01,588
抹黑您的部分呢?      抹黑回去
What about the smears against you personally? Smear him.

131
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:04,984
说他想重写历史 好显得他的治理
Say that he's trying to make his own premiership

132
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:07,465
不那么惨不忍睹
look a little less disastrous.

133
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:11,230
暗示他老糊涂了      好
Imply that he's going gaga. Fine.

134
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:16,428
"岁月流逝加上无据可查 也许模糊了他的记忆"
"Passage of time have perhaps clouded his memory."

135
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:22,197
好 老糊涂呢?      "对如此高龄的人不必苛责"
What about gaga? "One would expect it from a man of his age."

136
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,828
这就行了?      对 这章本身行了
That do? That's OK for the chapter.

137
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,790
那您想阻止出版的事呢?      说这也是谎话
What about your prevent publication? Say that's lies, too.

138
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:31,524
"这是对例会发言的断章取义"
"Garbled account of a routine meeting.

139
00:08:31,524 --> 00:08:33,246
"不存在封杀问题"      好
No question of suppression."

140
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,638
您要接受参访吗?      当然不要
Do you want to give interviews? No.

141
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,792
怎么解释呢?      引句原话
Shall I say why? Make it a quote.

142
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:42,906
"细枝末节 无关国是"
"Insignificant matter of no national importance.

143
00:08:42,906 --> 00:08:46,054
"媒体庸俗化政治的典型体现"
Typical of the media's trivialisation of politics."

144
00:08:46,054 --> 00:08:50,790
这话要归给谁?      亲密内阁同僚
And who shall I attribute that quote to? Close Cabinet colleague.

145
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,591
谢谢 首相
Thank you, Prime Minister.

146
00:08:55,880 --> 00:09:00,874
简直是灾难啊      当然没那么严重吧
This is a disaster. Oh, surely it's not all that serious.

147
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:04,669
还不严重? 跟公众说他们的首相不可信?
Telling the public they can't trust their Prime Minister?

148
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:08,150
他们才不会信呢
They won't believe that.

149
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:11,357
你觉得不会?      当然不会
Think not? Of course not.

150
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:15,149
也许会的 不然就是前首相不可信了
They might. Or they couldn't trust their ex-Prime Minister.

151
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,511
对 谢谢 伯纳
Yes, thank you.

152
00:09:16,511 --> 00:09:18,075
他们本来就不该信他
They never could trust him.

153
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:19,857
谢天谢地 还有我来重建
Thank goodness I've

154
00:09:19,857 --> 00:09:21,984
英国政坛的操守
brought back honesty.

155
00:09:21,984 --> 00:09:26,033
谢天谢地 首相      好 下面把泄漏钉起来
Thank goodness, Prime Minister. Now, about nailing that leak.

156
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,613
请原谅我的咬文嚼字
Sorry to be pedantic,

157
00:09:27,613 --> 00:09:29,852
可如果您钉上漏洞 就又开了个洞
but if you nail a leak, you make another.

158
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:37,245
我要追查出犯人      是 首相
I want to trace the culprit

159
00:09:37,245 --> 00:09:39,510
还要起诉他      是 首相
and I want a prosecution.

160
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:41,910
还要给他定罪
Yes, Prime Minister. And I want a conviction.

161
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:45,675
我们可以尽量追查犯人 也可以起诉
We can try and trace the culprit, we can prosecute,

162
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,831
但在现行政体之下
but under our political system,

163
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:52,710
政府恐怕很难包办定罪
there are problems about guaranteeing a conviction.

164
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:56,077
不会吧 跟法官喝点小酒?
Oh, surely. Little drinkie with the judge?

165
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:01,598
不可思议 绝对不可能对英国法官施压
Unthinkable. There is no way any pressure can be placed on a judge.

166
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,856
那怎么保证定罪?
How does one secure a conviction?

167
00:10:03,856 --> 00:10:06,475
很简单 找个不用施压的法官
Find a judge who won't need any pressure.

168
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:14,033
问问上院大法官 找个想做高级法官的
Find a judge who's hoping to be made a Lord of Appeal.

169
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:18,079
然后正义就自有公断了
Then leave justice to take her own impartial and majestic course.

170
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,435
这有用吗?      不一定
That does the trick? Not always.

171
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:26,391
有时他们太急于罗织罪名 陪审团就是狠心不让
they're so obviously, jury acquits out of bloody-mindedness.

172
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:30,109
还得找个有常识的法官      那当然
You need a judge with common sense. Oh, yes.

173
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:33,078
说起来容易找起来难啊
Won't be as easy as you make out.

174
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:39,232
好吧 你要我怎么跟读者说?
What are you asking me to tell my readers?

175
00:10:39,232 --> 00:10:41,390
我不是要你怎么说
I'm not asking you to tell them anything.

176
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,432
我只是给出我的说法
I'm just putting my side of the story.

177
00:10:43,432 --> 00:10:45,523
不至于吧 何必这么折腾呢
Why the big fuss?

178
00:10:45,523 --> 00:10:49,552
因为我不是双面人 我也没封杀那章
I have not got two faces and suppress that chapter.

179
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:52,314
能引你这句原话吗?      你不能引我
Can I quote you? You may not quote me

180
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:54,835
说我不是双面人那句
denying that I have two faces.

181
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:59,235
值得一试嘛 真不知你急什么 吉姆
It was worth a try. Dunno why you're so upset, Jim.

182
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:01,780
这章是没说你什么好话
The article doesn't exactly flatter you,

183
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:05,537
可在政坛上 这种事也是常有的吧
but it's part of the rough and tumble of political life.

184
00:11:05,537 --> 00:11:07,715
我真的觉得 负责任的媒体
A responsible newspaper

185
00:11:07,715 --> 00:11:09,629
不该登这种诽谤 你为什么登?
ought not to print such smears. Why did you?

186
00:11:09,629 --> 00:11:13,519
因为它让我们多卖了10万份
'Cause it sold us over 100,000 extra copies.

187
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:16,037
你不明白这种指控杀伤力多大吗?
Didn't you realise how damaging that accusation is?

188
00:11:16,037 --> 00:11:18,848
重点就在这 确实杀伤力不小
this is damaging.

189
00:11:18,848 --> 00:11:21,710
而你有权审查 你说你没想封杀它?
you didn't try to stop it?

190
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:23,219
我当然没有       为什么?
Of course I didn't.

191
00:11:23,219 --> 00:11:26,190
这是个自由国家 言论自由
It's a free country. Freedom of speech.

192
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:29,749
可它严重伤害你的名誉啊      倒也没那么重
It's damaging to you personally. Not that damaging.

193
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:34,516
那何必大费周章呢?      我关心的不是我个人的名誉
What's the fuss, then? It's not the damage to me personally I mind.

194
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:39,470
我是担心国家受的伤      国家?
It's the damage to Britain that I worry about. Britain?

195
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:42,590
贬损领导层会严重伤害国家威信
Undermining the leadership can damage the nation

196
00:11:42,590 --> 00:11:45,642
国际形象 英镑汇率等等
with foreigners, the pound.

197
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,825
我要你撤销关于封杀的报导
I want you to retract that suppression story. Hm.

198
00:11:51,675 --> 00:11:53,141
这可难了
I don't see how I can.

199
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:55,330
这有何难 你不是编辑吗?
Of course you can. You're the editor.

200
00:11:55,330 --> 00:11:58,689
对 可编辑不是军队总司令
I'm not a general commanding an army.

201
00:11:58,689 --> 00:12:01,750
我是马戏班班主 只管订演出
I'm the ringmaster of a circus. I book the acts,

202
00:12:01,750 --> 00:12:03,913
管不着杂耍艺人朝哪跳
but I can't tell the acrobats which way to jump!

203
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:11,390
我建议你 别显得太靠不住
It wouldn't be helpful to make us think we couldn't trust you.

204
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,894
我们当然乐意跟媒体合作
We'd like to cooperate with the press,

205
00:12:13,894 --> 00:12:16,387
但你这是为难我们
but you're making it difficult for us.

206
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:20,551
首相 我看是你最好别显得
I don't think it'd be helpful if you made it seem as

207
00:12:20,551 --> 00:12:23,367
成心和我们报纸过不去
though you were hostile to our paper.

208
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:27,116
我们当然乐意和10号合作 可如果要开战...
We like to cooperate with No.10, but if it's war...

209
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:31,273
不不不 我不是这意思...
No, no, no, no, no, I... No, I wasn't suggesting...

210
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,664
我只是说 我可以让你们
All I meant was that there could be

211
00:12:33,664 --> 00:12:36,761
做独家专访 独家拍照
exclusive interviews, photo opportunities...

212
00:12:36,761 --> 00:12:39,238
如果我撤销报导?      如果你报导真相
If I retract? If you print the truth.

213
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:42,101
吉姆 我不能改变口径
I have to stick by my story

214
00:12:42,101 --> 00:12:44,782
除非有确凿的反面证据
until I get hard evidence that it's not true.

215
00:12:44,782 --> 00:12:47,552
比如?      比如会议纪要
Such as? The minutes of the meeting.

216
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:52,628
我看没问题 事关我的清名啊      首相
I don't see why not. My integrity is at stake. Prime Minister...

217
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:56,839
伯纳 会议纪要和我说的一样 不是吗?
the minutes bear out my version of the meeting

218
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,673
这个 我...
Well, I... er... um...

219
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:03,116
这个 我...是的
Well, I... er... yes.

220
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,511
好 德雷克 会给你看的
Yes, Derek, you may see them.

221
00:13:04,511 --> 00:13:08,146
我知道事属机密 但这回情况特殊
I know they're usually confidential, but this is a special case.

222
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:12,712
能刊发吗?      再说吧 我先看一遍
Can I publish them? We'll see. I'll have another look at them.

223
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:15,872
伯纳 今天下午拿来给我
Bernard, show them to me this afternoon.

224
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,198
请进
Yes?

225
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,788
汉弗莱爵士       你好 伯纳
Sir Humphrey,  Yes, Bernard.

226
00:13:21,788 --> 00:13:23,812
能打扰一下吗?      好的 伯纳
have you got a moment?

227
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,394
我有麻烦了
Er... I've got a problem.

228
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,755
对 伯纳      您知道?
Yes, Bernard. You know?

229
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,512
对 伯纳      您怎么知道
Yes. How?

230
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:37,508
因为你刚告诉我了 伯纳
Because you've just told me.

231
00:13:37,508 --> 00:13:39,958
您知道我有什么麻烦吗?
Do you know what my problem is?

232
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:41,624
伯纳 你的麻烦是
Your problem is that

233
00:13:41,624 --> 00:13:43,582
你总说不到重点
you don't ever come to the point.

234
00:13:43,727 --> 00:13:46,621
是是 对不起 首相刚请
Sorry. The PM has just had lunch with

235
00:13:46,621 --> 00:13:48,063
德雷克伯汉吃了午餐 报社主编...
Derek Burnham, the editor...

236
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:51,078
我知道他是谁 伯纳      好 首相告诉他
I know who he is. The PM told him

237
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:56,030
内阁会议纪要证实 他没有试图查禁第8章
the minutes confirm that he didn't suppress chapter 8

238
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,794
若有必要 纪要会登报
and that he'd publish them if necessary.

239
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:03,158
那你有什么麻烦?      纪要还没写呢
So what is your problem? Well, the minutes aren't written yet.

240
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:06,596
我知道了      那...我该怎么办?
I see. So, er, what should I do?

241
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,556
去写啊 亲爱的伯纳
Write them, dear Bernard.

242
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,782
对 可问题是首相
The problem is the PM

243
00:14:12,782 --> 00:14:14,779
确实试图查禁那章了 不是吗?
did try to suppress the chapter, didn't he?

244
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:18,312
我不知道 是吗?      您不记得吗?
I don't know. Did he? Don't you remember?

245
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,649
我记得什么不重要 伯纳
What I remember is irrelevant.

246
00:14:20,649 --> 00:14:23,144
如果纪要没说他有 他就没有
If the minutes don't say that he did, then he didn't.

247
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:28,590
您想要我伪造会议纪要?      我绝对没这种想法
So you want me to falsify the minutes? I want nothing of the sort!

248
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,424
看你了 伯纳 你想要怎样?
What do YOU want, Bernard?

249
00:14:30,424 --> 00:14:32,071
我想有颗清白的良心
I want to have a clear conscience.

250
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:35,311
清白的良心      对
A clear conscience. Yes.

251
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:40,154
你几时有了这种奢侈的想法?
When did you acquire this taste for luxuries?

252
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:44,632
良心是留给政客的 伯纳
Consciences are for politicians, Bernard.

253
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,791
我们是卑微的社会公器
We are humble functionaries

254
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:50,953
职责不外乎贯彻民意代表的意志
duty is to implement  commands of representatives.

255
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:54,135
我们怎么可能错 如果我们
How could we be doing anything wrong if

256
00:14:54,135 --> 00:14:55,943
是在执行民意代表的命令?
it has been commanded by those representatives?

257
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,421
这我不能接受 汉弗莱爵士
I can't accept that.

258
00:14:57,421 --> 00:14:59,968
"没有人是孤岛"      正是 伯纳
No man is an island. I agree, Bernard.

259
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:03,352
"没有人是孤岛 没有人能自全"
"No man is an island, entire of itself;

260
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,715
"因此"
"And therefore

261
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:10,908
"别再问丧钟为谁而鸣"
"never send to know for whom the bell tolls."

262
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,548
"它正是为你敲响" 伯纳
It tolls for thee, Bernard.

263
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:15,917
那您看怎么办 汉弗莱爵士?
So what do you suggest, Sir Humphrey?

264
00:15:15,917 --> 00:15:20,773
伯纳 纪要不能面面俱到 对吗?
Minutes do not record everything, do they?

265
00:15:20,773 --> 00:15:21,379
对 当然不能
No, of course not.

266
00:15:21,379 --> 00:15:24,727
会议之中人们就会改变主意 对吗?
People change their minds during a meeting.

267
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,749
对       所以会议是
Yes... So the meeting is

268
00:15:26,749 --> 00:15:29,579
各种变数的集合体 由你选择
a mass of ingredients.

269
00:15:29,579 --> 00:15:33,518
就像烹饪加料      就像...不是像加料 伯纳
Oh, like cooking. Like... No, not like cooking, Bernard.

270
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:37,673
最好别用这词形容账本或者会议纪要
Better not use that word in connection with books or minutes.

271
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:42,231
你要从一堆杂乱无章的主张中
You choose from a jumble of ill-digested ideas

272
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:45,392
筛出一个版本 代表首相的观点
a version which represents the PM's views

273
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:49,336
也即他期望出现的那一种
as he would, on reflection, have liked them to emerge.

274
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:51,790
可如果记录不真实...
But if it's not a true record...

275
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:54,452
纪要的宗旨不在于记录事件本身
The purpose of minutes is not to record events,

276
00:15:54,452 --> 00:15:55,818
而在于保护当事人
it is to protect people.

277
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:02,114
你不能记录首相言不由衷的话
do not take notes if PM says something he did not mean to

278
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,795
尤其在这些话
particularly if it contradicts

279
00:16:03,795 --> 00:16:05,563
和他公开发言不一致的时候
something he has said publicly.

280
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:12,268
你要尽量完善他的话 提纲挈领 要讲策略
improve on what has been said, put it in a better order

281
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:15,830
可这怎么说得通呢?      你是他的仆人
But how do I justify that? You are his servant.

282
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:20,391
对啊      纪要是为留档做的记录
Oh, yes. A minute is a note for the records

283
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:24,348
也是共同决议的声明 如果真有决议的话
and a statement of action, if any, that was agreed upon.

284
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:28,513
会上发生了什么事?      讨论了那本书
What happened at the meeting? Well, the book was discussed.

285
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:33,151
副检察长提出 查禁它没有法律依据
The SG advised no legal grounds for suppressing

286
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:37,108
首相是否同意副检察长的话?
And did the PM accept what the Solicitor General had said?

287
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,953
他客观上同意
He accepted the fact there

288
00:16:38,953 --> 00:16:40,992
查禁没有法律依据 可...
were no legal grounds for suppression...

289
00:16:40,992 --> 00:16:43,435
他客观上同意
He accepted the fact

290
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:48,549
查禁没有法律依据 你看
that there were no legal grounds for suppression. You see?

291
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:53,995
这是撒谎吗?      不是
Is that a lie? No.

292
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,355
能写成会议纪要吗?      能
Can you write it in the minutes? Yes.

293
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:59,910
良心感觉如何?      好多了 谢谢您
How's your conscience? Much better, thank you.

294
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:07,777
伯纳伍列?       什么?
Bernard Woolley?

295
00:17:07,777 --> 00:17:09,478
你的会议纪要今天见报了
Your minutes were published today.

296
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:12,181
吉姆哈克和副检察长内阁会议的纪要
The minutes of Jim Hacker's meeting.

297
00:17:12,181 --> 00:17:13,723
对 我知道 我赶着上班
I know. I've got to go to work.

298
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:16,714
就回答几个问题      抱歉 我无可奉告
Answer a few questions. I can't comment.

299
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:19,501
可你得承认 事情非常可疑      什么?
But it all looks very suspicious. What?

300
00:17:19,501 --> 00:17:21,232
上周四就该发布的
Why did it take so long

301
00:17:21,232 --> 00:17:24,281
怎么拖了这么久?      因为它们没...
to publish them? Because they weren't...

302
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:26,869
没经过发布审查?
Weren't cleared for publication?

303
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:28,853
可首相上周四就审查了
But the PM cleared them last Thursday.

304
00:17:28,853 --> 00:17:32,956
对 可我们有<官方保密法>
Yes, but there's the Official Secrets Act.

305
00:17:32,956 --> 00:17:36,682
按照<官方保密法> 怎么能审查呢?
So how can they be cleared for publication?

306
00:17:36,682 --> 00:17:37,791
首相有权审查一切
The PM can clear anything.

307
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:42,033
你是说首相不受<官方保密法>约束?
Are you saying the PM is not subject to the Official Secrets Act?

308
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:45,954
这个...不      "不是"还是"确实不受"?
Well... no. No, he is or no, he isn't?

309
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:50,272
是      你是说规则由哈克说了算
Yes. You're saying that Hacker makes the rules.

310
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,396
不      可你就这么说的
No. That's what you said.

311
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:55,659
是      就是说在<官方保密法>上
Yes. So when it comes to the ACT

312
00:17:55,659 --> 00:17:57,366
首相凌驾于法律之上
the Prime Minister is above the law.

313
00:17:57,366 --> 00:17:59,674
理论上不是      可实践中呢?
Not in theory. But in practice?

314
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,395
无可奉告      真有意思 伯纳
No comment. Very interesting.

315
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:07,517
听着 我觉得我没有说清楚
Look, I'm not sure I've made myself clear.

316
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,910
你已经说得够清楚了      对了还有
Oh, you've made it very clear.

317
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:12,381
能不能证实一下
Any truth in the rumour that

318
00:18:12,381 --> 00:18:13,963
你的纪要花了四天才见报
your minutes took four days to appear

319
00:18:13,963 --> 00:18:14,612
是因为哈克先生
because Mr Hacker

320
00:18:14,612 --> 00:18:16,857
只会用两个指头打字?
can only type with two fingers?

321
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,471
抱歉失陪 我真得走了
Excuse me, I must go.

322
00:18:23,114 --> 00:18:26,669
对了 我这些是非官方发言
Oh... er... by the way, I was speaking off the record.

323
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:29,229
抱歉 伯纳 现在说有点晚了
Sorry, a bit late to say that now.

324
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,880
首相      什么 伯纳?
Prime Minister. Yes, Bernard?

325
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:41,032
能打扰一下吗?      好的 伯纳
Have you got a moment? Yes, Bernard.

326
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,998
我有个麻烦了
Er... I've got a problem.

327
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,999
说吧 伯纳      呃...是这样
Get on with it, Bernard. Er... yes.

328
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:55,720
我刚接受了媒体采访
I've just been interviewed by the press.

329
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:59,589
你? 接受采访?      对 恐怕是的
You? You gave an interview? Er, yes, I'm afraid so.

330
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:01,281
这事不归你做      我知道
That's not your job. I couldn't help it.

331
00:19:01,281 --> 00:19:04,423
我也没办法啊...就那么发生了
I just... It just happened.

332
00:19:04,423 --> 00:19:07,710
他们包围我 我不得不说      你说了什么?
They trapped me into speaking to them. What did you say?

333
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:11,475
其实没什么      那你有什么麻烦?
Nothing, really. Well, what's your problem?

334
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:15,838
他们问我您的事      我的什么事?
They were asking me about you. What about me?

335
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,389
关于您和<官方保密法>      还有呢?
About the Official Secrets Act. And?

336
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:21,279
关于您是否受它约束      我当然受
Whether you were bound by it. Of course I am!

337
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,182
对 您当然受
Of course you are, but it...

338
00:19:22,182 --> 00:19:25,804
可报导...也许不会这么写
it might not come out like that.

339
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:30,271
你什么意思?
What do you mean?

340
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:33,346
回想一下我说过的 还有他们说的
Thinking back on what I said and what they said

341
00:19:33,346 --> 00:19:35,042
还有我说您说过的
and what I said you said

342
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,463
还有他们可能会说我说您说过的
and what they may say I said you said

343
00:19:37,463 --> 00:19:39,563
或者他们可能会觉得
or what they may have thought

344
00:19:39,563 --> 00:19:40,970
我说过我觉得的您的观点
I said I thought you thought,

345
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,712
他们也许会说 我说我觉得
they may say I said I thought

346
00:19:43,712 --> 00:19:45,561
您说您觉得...
you said you thought...

347
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,868
说呀 伯纳
Go on, Bernard.

348
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,711
我想我说了 您说您觉得
Well, I think I said you said you thought

349
00:19:53,711 --> 00:19:55,285
您凌驾于法律之上
you were above the law.

350
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:58,350
你说了那种话?
You said that?!

351
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:01,327
不是故意的 就那么脱口而出了
Not intentionally. It's just the way it came out.

352
00:20:01,327 --> 00:20:03,820
真对不起 他们拿问题轰炸我
They were asking me all these questions.

353
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:06,291
伯纳 就算别人提问
What makes you think

354
00:20:06,291 --> 00:20:07,410
谁告诉你非回答不可的?
you have to answer them?

355
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:11,389
我不知道      我提问你就从来不答啊
I don't know. You've never answered my questions!

356
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:14,552
我知道...      做了一辈子公务员
I know... After a lifetime in the Civil Service,

357
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,712
整个职业生涯都在回避问题
a career devoted to avoiding questions,

358
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:21,350
你突然决定今天有问必答 而且是对媒体
you suddenly decide to answer them today and to the press?!

359
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:23,636
你脑袋进水了吧 伯纳
You must have flipped your lid!

360
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:26,994
请别冲我吼 首相 我向您保证
Please don't shout at me! I assure you,

361
00:20:26,994 --> 00:20:29,247
我再也不回答任何问题了
I won't answer questions ever again!

362
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:32,709
叫汉弗莱和比尔过来
Get Humphrey and Bill in here.

363
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:37,832
去请汉弗莱爵士 还有比尔普雷查德
Send Sir Humphrey in and Bill Pritchard.

364
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,712
如果再碰上这种情况 伯纳
If this question should ever arise again,

365
00:20:40,712 --> 00:20:43,094
你要这样对付提问
this is how you deal with questions.

366
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:46,028
如果无话可说 就说无可奉告
If you have nothing to say, say nothing.

367
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:48,238
最好是有话可说
Better still, have something to say

368
00:20:48,238 --> 00:20:50,247
并且说出来 不管他们问什么
and say it, no matter what they ask.

369
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:54,069
不必在乎问题 只管发表你的意见
Pay no attention to the question. Just make your own statement.

370
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:56,078
如果他们重提那个问题
If they ask the question again,

371
00:20:56,078 --> 00:20:58,452
就说"问题不在这里"
you say, "That's not the question"

372
00:20:58,452 --> 00:21:00,736
或者"我认为真正问题在于..."
or "I think the real question is..." and then

373
00:21:00,736 --> 00:21:03,877
然后再发表一通你的意见
you make another statement of your own.

374
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:06,666
泄密调查进展如何?
How's that leak inquiry coming on?

375
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:10,631
首相 程序马上就开始运转
The wheels will be turning very soon.

376
00:21:10,631 --> 00:21:13,074
马上? 我都交待了一星期了
I asked you a week ago!

377
00:21:13,074 --> 00:21:14,346
你们俩怎么回事?
What's the matter with you two?

378
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:17,952
真抱歉 首相 我不知道您是认真的
I'm sorry, I had no idea you were serious.

379
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:23,509
泄密调查一般不会认真追查
Leak inquiries are not usually pursued.

380
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:27,275
我要这次认真追查 并且立即启动
I want this one pursued rigorously and immediately!

381
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:29,829
认真追查?      并且立即启动
Rigorously? And immediately.

382
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,992
立即启动?      立即启动
Immediately? Immediately.

383
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:36,152
您是说您真要查出泄密人?
You mean you REALLY want it pursued?

384
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:37,196
看我的嘴形 汉弗莱
Watch the lips move, Humphrey.

385
00:21:37,196 --> 00:21:40,259
我要求认真追查 立即启动
I want it pursued. Now.

386
00:21:40,259 --> 00:21:43,630
遵命 首相 如果您是说真的
Very well, Prime Minister, if you're serious.

387
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:48,112
我会组织真正的调查 如果您真想这么办
I will arrange a genuine inquiry if that's what you really want.

388
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:51,875
我去找特工处的普劳德探长      谢谢
I'll get Inspector Plod of the Special Branch. Thank you.

389
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:54,755
我们得想点办法 搞好和媒体的关系
We must do something to improve my relations with the press,

390
00:21:54,755 --> 00:21:58,207
它今天刚严重恶化了
which deteriorated considerably

391
00:21:58,242 --> 00:22:02,190
因为我的私人秘书告诉他们 我自以为
when my private secretary told them I felt

392
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:04,222
在官方保密问题上凌驾于法律之上
I was above the law when it came to official secrets.

393
00:22:04,320 --> 00:22:06,834
对 你知道低头就好 伯纳
Yes, you may well hang your head.

394
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,048
宪法上怎么排位的 汉弗莱?
What's the constitutional position, Humphrey?

395
00:22:11,048 --> 00:22:14,043
首相 从某种意义上说 伯纳没错
Well, in a sense, Bernard was right.

396
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:18,117
简而言之 问题在于如何区分
The question, in a nutshell, is what is the difference

397
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:21,317
违反<官方保密法>的行为
between a breach of the Official Secrets Act

398
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:25,792
和某高级官员做的匿名非正式简报
unattributable, off-the-record briefing by official?

399
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:29,031
前者 即违反法律 是一项罪名
The former a breach is a criminal offence.

400
00:22:29,031 --> 00:22:32,595
而后者 即简报 却是必要的工作手段
A briefing is essential to keep the wheels turning.

401
00:22:32,595 --> 00:22:34,236
二者之间是有实质区别呢
Is there a difference or is it a matter

402
00:22:34,236 --> 00:22:36,503
还是模棱两可 随心所欲?
of convenience and interpretation?

403
00:22:36,503 --> 00:22:38,796
一次违法行为 可不可能基于
Is it a breach of the act if there is an

404
00:22:38,796 --> 00:22:43,015
一名官员做的匿名非官方简报
unofficial, non-attributable briefing by an official who's been

405
00:22:43,015 --> 00:22:45,385
并且有首相的非官方授权?
unofficially authorised by the Prime Minister?

406
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:49,633
有首相授权的当然不是      我就是这么说的
Not if it's been authorised by the PM, no. That's what I say.

407
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:51,056
我当然应该有权决定
I should decide if it's

408
00:22:51,056 --> 00:22:53,541
揭露什么才符合国家利益
in the national interest for something

409
00:22:53,541 --> 00:22:55,860
问题是 官员没这个权力
to be disclosed, not officials.

410
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,467
上周泄密的祸首是一名官员
Last week's leak must've come from an official.

411
00:22:58,467 --> 00:23:01,054
可如果这名官员有官方授权
But what if the official was officially authorised

412
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:03,870
甚或是非官方授权呢?
or even unofficially authorised?

413
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:08,147
如果首相发表官方反对
What if the PM officially disapproves of a breach

414
00:23:08,147 --> 00:23:10,254
非官方场合又支持呢?
of the act, but unofficially approves?

415
00:23:10,254 --> 00:23:12,458
那么这就是一次非官方的官方泄密
then it will be unofficially official,

416
00:23:12,458 --> 00:23:13,829
却是官方的非官方泄密
but officially unofficial.

417
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:18,157
多谢 汉弗莱 你帮了大忙了      多谢 首相
Thank you. You've been a tremendous help. Thank you.

418
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:20,032
好吧 现在要想法补救
Now, we've got to do something to repair

419
00:23:20,032 --> 00:23:22,557
你们两个本周给我惹的祸
the damage you two have done to me.

420
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:26,590
我最好再找个主编吃顿饭 找个友好点的
I'd better have lunch with another editor, a friendlier one.

421
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:27,894
容我打断一下 首相
None of them are

422
00:23:27,894 --> 00:23:30,418
恐怕眼下他们都不大友好
friendly at the moment.

423
00:23:30,418 --> 00:23:33,508
不能给他们个爵位吗?
Couldn't we offer one of them a knighthood?

424
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:38,565
送人爵位是把双刃剑 对您可好可坏
That can work for or against you.

425
00:23:38,565 --> 00:23:41,019
得看您给了之后 还能否控制他们
Do you have any control over them once you've given it?

426
00:23:41,019 --> 00:23:43,118
哪个编辑都会很高兴吧
Wouldn't they be pleased?

427
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:47,479
但有了爵位 他们更可能乱说了 百无禁忌了
he may feel free to say what he likes. Nothing to lose.

428
00:23:47,479 --> 00:23:50,071
没错 别指望事后收获感激之情
You don't get gratitude afterwards.

429
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:51,724
感激不外乎是
Gratitude is merely a lively

430
00:23:51,724 --> 00:23:54,425
对将来好处的热切期盼
expectation of favours to come.

431
00:23:55,800 --> 00:24:00,191
依我看 与其讨好媒体 不如转移他们注意力?
May I suggest that we distract the press?

432
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:02,510
我们给他们个故事      比如说?
Let's give them a story. Such as?

433
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:04,989
发动个战争之类的
Start a war, that sort of thing.

434
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:09,834
发动战争?      小战争就行
Start a war?! Only a small war.

435
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,919
容我打断一下
Um... if I might intervene.

436
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:16,799
就算小战争可能也过火了
Even a small war would be overkill.

437
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:22,837
您何不驱逐76名苏联外交官员呢?
Why don't you expel 76 Soviet diplomats?

438
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,012
这是惯例 每次我们
That's always been our practice when we wish

439
00:24:26,536 --> 00:24:29,886
想转移媒体注意力都这么办
to ensure the press lose interest in something.

440
00:24:29,886 --> 00:24:32,035
我不能这样      您会上头条
I can't do that. Great headline.

441
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:35,192
"政府大破赤色间谍网" 多爱国
"Government cracks down on red spy ring." Very patriotic.

442
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:36,948
一定得是没人能否认的消息
It must be a story that nobody can disprove.

443
00:24:36,948 --> 00:24:41,150
就算被否认人们也相信
And which will be believed even if it's denied.

444
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:45,871
"苏联大使司机乃是克格勃中将"
"Soviet ambassador's chauffeur is Lieutenant General in KGB."

445
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:50,110
我不能这样 我花了几周辛辛苦苦缓和局势
I can't do that. I've been working at this detente for weeks.

446
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:53,272
这是眼下唯一有进展的工作
It's the only thing that IS working at the moment.

447
00:24:53,440 --> 00:24:57,831
你说呢 伯纳? 你不是爆料专家吗
What do you think? You're good at getting in the papers.

448
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,434
皇家事件如何?      比如呢?
What about a royal event? Such as?

449
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:04,434
订婚 离婚 或者怀孕
An engagement, a divorce, a pregnancy.

450
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:10,029
你能安排吗?
You can arrange that?

451
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:16,811
他读泄密调查报告了吗?
Has he read the leak inquiry report?

452
00:25:16,811 --> 00:25:19,244
他正在读 我们怎么办?
Yes. How do we handle it?

453
00:25:19,244 --> 00:25:22,174
很难办 泄密调查查出责任人
Very difficult. There is almost no precedent for

454
00:25:22,174 --> 00:25:25,098
几乎没有先例可循
handling a leak inquiry which finds the culprit.

455
00:25:25,098 --> 00:25:27,666
更别说责任人还是高级公务员
Especially when it's a senior civil servant.

456
00:25:27,666 --> 00:25:29,319
不过我看我们能救他
I think we can save him.

457
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:33,230
怎么救? 他出席会议了 他招认了
How? He was at the meeting. He's owned up.

458
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:37,598
就是他干的 毫无疑问 对吗?      会有疑问的
There can't be any doubt. There's going to be.

459
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:46,359
汉弗莱 看到了吗? 被我猜中了
There, Humphrey, you see? Just as I suspected.

460
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:48,806
我要起诉那个能源部新闻秘书
I want that press officer at the Department of Energy prosecuted.

461
00:25:48,806 --> 00:25:50,457
根据官方保密法...
The official secret act...

462
00:25:50,457 --> 00:25:52,792
恕我反对 首相      你反对是吗 汉弗莱?
I think not... You think not?

463
00:25:52,792 --> 00:25:54,586
就因为他是公务员?
Because he's a civil servant?

464
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:55,857
当然不是 首相
No, PRIME MINISTER

465
00:25:55,857 --> 00:25:57,538
是因为这违反您的利益
because it is not in your interests.

466
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,882
违反我的利益? 惩办一个
That somebody should be punished for

467
00:25:59,882 --> 00:26:02,148
把政府贬得一钱不值的人?
undermining government?

468
00:26:02,176 --> 00:26:03,991
首相 副检察长
The Attorney General

469
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:06,914
说不可能成功起诉
says that a prosecution would not succeed

470
00:26:06,914 --> 00:26:09,581
因为不涉及安全问题
because there are no security implications.

471
00:26:09,581 --> 00:26:11,675
我不管 就当杀鸡儆猴吧
At least it'd make an example of him.

472
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:14,182
他还建议 如果我们起诉
He advises that if we prosecute, we must

473
00:26:14,182 --> 00:26:17,208
我们必须也请特工处调查
undertake a similar Special Branch inquiry

474
00:26:17,208 --> 00:26:18,357
早先第5章的泄露
into the earlier leak of chapter 5

475
00:26:18,357 --> 00:26:20,908
您知道 您在库朗的成就
your success in Kumran.

476
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:24,397
这个...完全是两码事
Ah... well... that was completely different.

477
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:27,597
何以见得?      那个完全无害嘛
May one ask why? Well, it was harmless.

478
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:31,912
副检察长说要么两次都无害 要么都有害
AG says that either both are harmless or neither.

479
00:26:32,080 --> 00:26:35,516
要我去通知特工处 调查第5章的泄露吗?
Shall I ask Special Branch to work on the chapter 5 leak?

480
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:38,877
好吧 不起诉了 炒掉那新闻秘书
Drop the prosecution, but sack the press officer.

481
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:42,287
这也很难 有证据显示
That could be difficult. There is evidence

482
00:26:42,287 --> 00:26:44,492
他不是自作主张
he was not acting on his own initiative.

483
00:26:44,492 --> 00:26:47,352
怎么讲?      是他上司国务大臣的授意
Meaning? They were his Secretary of State's wishes.

484
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:49,450
什么?      对 显然
What?! Yes

485
00:26:49,450 --> 00:26:51,084
国务大臣很乐意
The Secretary was not displeased

486
00:26:51,084 --> 00:26:55,398
被写成内阁最能干的大臣 他吩咐新闻秘书
at being described as the ablest minister

487
00:26:55,560 --> 00:27:01,351
他不仅不想封杀这一章 还希望它马上见报
 he wouldn't mind seeing it in the press at once.

488
00:27:01,520 --> 00:27:05,308
并且提到 它只能如此面世
With reference to the fact that it might not otherwise be read

489
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:09,314
因为10号施压要查禁它      你肯定吗?
because of an attempt by No.10 to censor it. You sure of this?

490
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:13,473
我肯定那位新闻秘书会这么解释
I am sure that's what the press officer's explanation will be

491
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:15,029
当他以非法解雇为名
when his case for wrongful dismissal

492
00:27:15,029 --> 00:27:17,584
起诉到劳工法庭的时候
comes up before the industrial tribunal.

493
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:19,738
非法解雇?      他会辩解说
Wrongful dismissal? He'll argue

494
00:27:19,738 --> 00:27:22,327
他是执行暗示的命令
he was following an implied order.

495
00:27:22,327 --> 00:27:24,665
实行他的国务大臣的授意
Carrying out his Secretary of State's wishes.

496
00:27:24,665 --> 00:27:26,724
所以我也不能炒他      不能
So I can't sack him.

497
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:31,951
那我能炒谁?      首相 如果您非要炒掉谁
Well, who can I sack? Well, if you must sack somebody,

498
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:34,657
唯一人选是能源大臣
the only candidate is the Energy Secretary

499
00:27:34,657 --> 00:27:36,578
他要为他的部负责
who is responsible for his department.

500
00:27:36,578 --> 00:27:39,810
这怎么行 我上周刚失去一名大臣
I can't do that. I lost one minister last week.

501
00:27:39,810 --> 00:27:41,295
不能这周又炒一个吧
I can't sack another this week.

502
00:27:41,295 --> 00:27:45,686
正是 首相 失去一名内阁大臣
Quite, Prime Minister. To lose one Cabinet minister

503
00:27:45,686 --> 00:27:46,919
可以看作不幸
may be regarded as a misfortune.

504
00:27:46,919 --> 00:27:50,192
失去两个就像是识人不明了
To lose both looks like carelessness.

505
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:56,438
谢谢 伯纳 还有 首相
Thank you, Bernard. Furthermore, Prime Minister,

506
00:27:56,600 --> 00:28:00,741
能源大臣没有泄密 也没授意泄密
as the Energy Secretary did not do the leaking,

507
00:28:00,741 --> 00:28:03,111
他也可以告我们非法解雇
he might sue for wrongful dismissal as well.

508
00:28:03,111 --> 00:28:06,436
那我怎么办? 媒体都吵着要调查结果
The press is clamouring for the result of this inquiry.

509
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:10,673
新闻办...起草了这份声明
Well, the press office... has drafted this statement.

510
00:28:13,480 --> 00:28:17,678
"通讯故障...误解..."
"Communications breakdown... misunderstanding...

511
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:22,436
"...动机是好的...将以内部规章处理"
"will be dealt with by internal procedures."

512
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,113
这是漂白      不不 不完全是
This is a whitewash. Not really.

513
00:28:25,113 --> 00:28:27,262
它把责任平摊了
It shares out the blame equally.

514
00:28:27,262 --> 00:28:29,709
可以称之为漂灰
More of a grey wash.

515
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:33,622
看着还是像我要查禁它
Still looks like I tried to suppress that chapter.

516
00:28:33,622 --> 00:28:35,136
我该怎么办 汉弗莱?
What am I to do?

517
00:28:35,136 --> 00:28:37,592
也许我们应该把消息公开
Perhaps we should send the story out,

518
00:28:38,177 --> 00:28:39,932
然后扼杀它
but smother it.

519
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:43,558
扼杀它? 你是说...
Smother it? You mean...

520
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:47,759
首相 我正打算告诉您
Oh, Prime Minister, I've been meaning to tell you.

521
00:28:47,920 --> 00:28:51,553
外交部文件里有些消息很让人担心
There's some very worrying information on the Foreign Office files

522
00:28:51,553 --> 00:28:54,236
是关于苏联使馆
about espionage in the Soviet embassy

523
00:28:54,236 --> 00:28:56,629
和贸易代表团的间谍活动
and trade delegation.

524
00:28:56,800 --> 00:29:01,157
不会吧      有不利证据指向许多外交官员
No? Evidence against a lot of diplomats.

525
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:03,791
多少?
How many?

526
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:05,951
76位
76

527
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:10,910
汉弗莱 我看是该铁腕一下了
You know, I think the time has come to be firm.

528
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:14,470
毫无疑问      这关系到领土主权问题
Absolutely. The defence of the realm is at stake.

529
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:16,761
千真万确      驱逐他们
Precisely. Expel them.

530
00:29:16,761 --> 00:29:19,007
我要媒体今天就得到消息
And I want the press told today.

531
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:22,268
同时进行
At the same time...

532
00:29:22,440 --> 00:29:24,431
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

533
00:29:25,961 --> 00:29:35,570
